.TH SKYAPO-BENCH 1 "2026-10-01" "SkyAPO 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skyapo-bench \- measure SkyAPO DSP block processing time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skyapo-bench
--config \fIFILE\fR [--rate \fIHZ\fR] [--channels \fICOUNT\fR]
[--block \fIFRAMES\fR] [--warmup \fIBLOCKS\fR]
[--iterations \fIBLOCKS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B skyapo-bench
loads a SkyAPO configuration into the same DSP engine used by the offline
renderer and measures repeated fixed-size processing blocks. Configuration
loading and input-buffer preparation are outside the timed interval. Results
are emitted as one JSON object with mean, median, p95 and maximum block time
alongside the nominal block budget.
.PP
The JSON also includes process peak RSS in KiB. This includes the executable,
loaded libraries and runtime state; it is not an isolated measurement of the
filter graph's allocation.
.PP
This measures the local DSP engine only. It does not measure PipeWire graph
latency, scheduling jitter, device latency, or callback overhead,
and it is not a realtime-safety guarantee.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config \fIFILE\fR
Configuration to validate, construct and process. Required.
.TP
.B --rate \fIHZ\fR
Nominal sample rate. Default: 48000.
.TP
.B --channels \fICOUNT\fR
Channel count from 1 through 8. Default: 2.
.TP
.B --block \fIFRAMES\fR
Frames in each measured block. Default: 256.
.TP
.B --warmup \fIBLOCKS\fR
Unmeasured warmup blocks. Default: 500.
.TP
.B --iterations \fIBLOCKS\fR
Measured blocks. Default: 5000.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
skyapo-bench --config examples/basic.txt --rate 48000 --channels 2 --block 256
.fi
